WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome, everybody.
Thank you so much.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.336
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:06.372
Let's get to the news
and jokes, please.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.307
Well guys, tonight was
the first night

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.376
of the Democratic
National Convention.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.246
It was pretty different from
what we've seen in the past.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.015 line:0%
-An unprecedented
Democratic National Convention

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.885 line:0%
will begin at what will be
an almost entirely

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.252 line:0%
virtual event.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.589 line:0%
The party will officially
nominate Joe Biden

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.658 line:0%
and Kamala Harris to lead
the presidential ticket.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.660
-Yeah, it was the first night
of the virtual

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.695
Democratic National Convention,

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.631
because nothing quite
fires up Americans

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.633
like long speeches over Zoom.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.301
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.237
That's right, both the
Democratic and Republican

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.972
National Conventions
will be held without crowds,

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:42.275
which is a bummer because
the best part of these things

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.110
isn't the speeches,
it's the people in the crowds

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.611
dancing like idiots.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:51.551
♪♪

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.885
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.188
♪♪

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.556
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.725
♪♪

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.028
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.896
-I like that.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.832
For the first night of
the Democratic Convention

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.968
there was wall-to-wall
coverage on CNN and MSNBC.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.771
Meanwhile, on Fox News,
there was a three-hour special

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.741
called "Kamala Harris: Where
Do You Think She Was Born?"

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.242
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.977
Each night of the convention
has its own theme.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.146
For example, tonight's theme
was "We the People."

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.880
Tomorrow night is
"Leadership Matters,"

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.484
and Wednesday is, "Please Don't
Switch to Netflix."

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.952
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.586
Well, earlier tonight
Bernie Sanders gave

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.188
a virtual speech
at the convention.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.490
It was pretty exciting.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.359
While Bernie's speech was
streaming live, so was he.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.593
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.028
-Oh!

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.531
[ Laughing continues ]

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.766
-It was weird seeing Bernie
do a virtual speech.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.936
He ended up by going,
"That's my speech,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.305
be sure to smash
that like button.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.439
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.942
Gucci!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.576
But the biggest speaker
of the night was

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.411
former First Lady
Michelle Obama.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:53.846
Her message was pretty simple.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:57.049
She was like, "Please win so
I don't have to run in 2024.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.651
Please."

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.353
If you missed Michelle Obama's
speech, don't worry,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.688
Melania will deliver
the same speech at next week's

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.957
Republican convention.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.958
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.027
Well, the virtual convention
rolls on tomorrow,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.962
and even though it's all
happening remotely,

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.764
it still looks like
an exciting night.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.799
Here's the schedule.
First at 9:00,

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:17.469
remarks from former acting
Attorney General Sally Yates.

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:19.139
Then at 9:30, remarks from

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.841
Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.910
Then at 10:00, remarks from
Senator Chuck Schumer.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.213
Then at 10:01, a break
to help Chuck Schumer

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.082
reconnect his Wifi.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.617
Then at 10:02, Schumer calls
his daughter to ask

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.519
for the Wifi password,
but she doesn't answer,

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:36.122
so he leaves a message asking
how to send a text.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.957
[ Laughter ]
Next at 10:03,

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.393
FaceTime between I.T. guy
and Schumer,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.361
where Schumer holds the
phone up to his ear

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:45.097
because he doesn't realize
it's a video call.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.867
10:05, Schumer reconnects,
but it's using his cellphone,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.768
not his Wifi, so he panics

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:52.005
because he doesn't have
unlimited data.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.740
10:07, Schumer says he's
restarting the router

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.776
while actually just turning on
a dehumidifier.

00:02:57.776 --> 00:02:59.879
Finally at 10:10, Bernie Sanders
comes on and says,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.814
"Oh, the hell with him,
I'll speak again."

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.449
So, sounds like a big night.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.617
Well, the other big story right
now is the postal service.

00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:07.019
People are worried
that budget cuts

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:09.322
are going to hurt mail-in
voting -- watch this.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.790 line:0%
-Friday, a number
of states reported

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.292 line:0%
officials got letters from
the Postal Service warning them

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:15.862 line:0%
the agency will not be able
to fulfill requests

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.431 line:0%
for mail-in ballots in time
for this November's election.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.333
-Trump was like, "Hey,
if the states got those letters

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.736
from the Postal Service,
how bad could it be?"

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.506
This is crazy. We can't send in
mail-in ballots?

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.507
Meanwhile, Americans can get
drunk, go on Amazon,

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.476
and eight hours later there's
a new pair of sunglasses

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.311
for their ferret waiting
at their front door.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:35.080
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.816
But in response to all this,
Nancy Pelosi

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.517
and her fellow Democrats
are fighting back.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:39.685
Listen to this.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.220 line:0%
-House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
announced

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.655 line:0%
she is calling back lawmakers
from their summer recess

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:46.325 line:0%
to deal with the crisis
at the Postal Service.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.260 line:0%
House Democrats have launched
an investigation over

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.230 line:0%
whether the Trump administration
is intentionally undermining

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.100 line:0%
the agency ahead of the
presidential election.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.102
-That's right. The House is
cutting its vacation short

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.536
to deal with this.

00:03:57.536 --> 00:03:59.372
When they heard lawmakers were
flying back to Washington,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.639
the Postal Service was like,

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.208
"Would you mind bringing
this sack of mail?"

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.742
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:05.711
You know 2020 is crazy
when Congressional hearings

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:09.081
about the Postal Service
are must-see TV.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.350
Meanwhile, Trump held
a press conference

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.685
from his Bedminster
Golf Club on Saturday

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.054
and bragged about the enthusiasm
for his campaign

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.089
from a strange
voting block.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.058
-I just looked.
There are thousands of boats

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.993
in lakes, rivers and oceans.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:23.963
Thousands and thousands
of boats.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.664
It's called Boaters for Trump.

00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:28.434
Boaters for Trump/Pence.
There's signs all over.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.470
Some of the boats have
ten flags on them.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.671
They're incredible.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:34.140
Because everyone knows
all elections come down

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.642
to the boater vote.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:37.943
[ As Trump ]
"I love all boaters.

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:39.745
And remember to boat for me
on Election Day.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.347
Every boat counts, so..."

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.781
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:45.652
Meanwhile, Trump is still angry
about his news coverage.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:49.188
Yesterday he tweeted that people
should, "Start watching OANN,"

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.823
a right-wing cable channel

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.791
known for spreading
conspiracy theories.

00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:54.427
Well, they have some very
interesting shows,

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.329
and you can tell that
they're fans of Trump.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.498
For example, there's
"White-ish."

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.199
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:03.469
Next up, there's
"The Marvelous Mr. Mnuchin."

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.805
Next there's, "How Mike Pence
Met Mother."

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.506
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.042
And, finally, there's
"Orange Mirror."

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.044
That's a good lineup.
Good lineup.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:13.746
Oh, here's some good news.
It looks like there's

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.881
a new COVID test on the way
that could be a game changer.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.016
Check it out.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.350
-Federal Officials
have just given

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.219
emergency approval
to what's being called

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.221
"a groundbreaking
new saliva test."

00:05:23.221 --> 00:05:26.625
It was developed by researchers
at Yale University.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:29.895
The test, expected to cost
just 10 bucks.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.430
You're also expected
to get results

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.666
in a matter of hours,
not days.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.169
-Yeah. The new tests will
make it extra weird

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.703
when patients show up, like,

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.173
"Nah, I prefer the cotton swab
straight to the brain, please."

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.440
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.775
Yeah, you can take
the test at home,

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.176
or if you're in a hurry,

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:47.212
just go to the spitting section
of the Walmart pharmacy.

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.415
And, finally, this is crazy,
I heard about a 12-year-old

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.083
in Australia who was just caught

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.618
doing something
pretty unexpected.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:53.786
Watch this.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.821 line:0%
-Three minors were caught
gambling

00:05:55.821 --> 00:06:00.460 line:0%
at an Australian casino,
including a 12-year-old girl.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.161
-Yeah. The girl was like,
[ Deep voice ]

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.863
"It ain't gambling when
you have a system."

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:08.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.801
Even weirder, her dad
was across the street

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.704
in a ball pit at
Chuck E. Cheese.

